<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dahlak Kebir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dahlak Kebir is the largest island of the Dahlak Archipelago in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massawa">Massawa</a>. From the 10th century it was the seat of a Muslim sultanate that controlled the sea approaches to the Ethiopian coast. Its cemeteries, with hundreds of Arabic tombstones, and its many cisterns are among the main medieval Islamic remains in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dahlak-kebir.jpg" alt="Dahlak Kebir" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amod Photography · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wrecks_on_Dahlak_Island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
